            "The actual True/pipe row publicly creates a consecutive-failure monitor, reports one Success/Skipped/ExpectedCancellation and a matching Failed callback binding outcome, then records actual failed handler/cleanup and settlement facts. CaptureSnapshot yields successful=failed=skipped=expectedCanceled=consecutiveFailures=1, countersSaturated=false, lastOutcome=Failed, state=Unhealthy; execution42 is Settled, both secondary statuses Failed, all observed durations positive and all applicable errors/times populated. The adopted C04 collection seam adds a settled optional diagnostic. FormatPipeResponse supplies the complete detailed envelope to ParseResponse before JSON-field assertions.",
            "C03/C05 admit those public facts and require the detached complete snapshot; C06 detailed fields mirror that snapshot and preserve actual outcome/secondary/timing facts; C08 admits the matching complete version1 detailed response through the real probe ParseResponse boundary. This is produced from real public runtime facts, not an arbitrary detached DTO or an invented invalid business duration.",
